93
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:16,980
Yes.

94
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:19,260
So yeah, small informal restaurant.

95
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,820
Yeah, bistro.

96
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:25,840
Okay, so our third phrase for today is not all that crazy about.

97
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:28,200
Not all that crazy about.

98
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:31,140
I'm not all that crazy about.

99
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:37,840
Okay, again, kind of a funny phrase, but we've got some examples that will help you understand the meaning.

100
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:40,420
Example one.

101
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:45,730
Do you want to go shopping with me tomorrow?

102
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:48,330
I'm not all that crazy about shopping.

103
00:04:48,730 --> 00:04:49,630
I don't like spending money.

104
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:54,840
Example two.

105
00:04:58,330 --> 00:05:00,130
I'm not crazy about jazz music.

106
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:01,270
Can I change the song?

107
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:08,480
So this is just a really polite way of saying you don't like something.

108
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:09,100
Exactly.

109
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,620
But now the opposite of this would be tasty.

110
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:13,560
Tasty.

111
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,520
That's our fourth word, tasty.

112
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,260
Tasty.

113
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,460
So when something is tasty, it's good.

114
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:20,180
